    "Flat high core exterior includes the adjacent room/service band rather than mistaking stair center for external shell.614 west recessed porch/stair and621 inset southern entrance are distinct; source-backed6211F northern room band restored instead of invented full undercroft.",
    "621 curved-core attached landing, connecting flight, complete broad exterior stair and immediate natural landings retained. Exact direction/riser count/levels are approximations. Far narrow rounded outside route not forced to connect to low-wing end room; omitted at natural interface, not halfway down treads.",
    "610 high south facade preserves broad blank mass, limited middle openings, grouped upper bands and bounded raised central roof cap rather than uniform five-window rows.611 existing straight-edged6F end wall carries local arch proxy. Earlier mandatory identification of611 arch as610 curved core is explicitly withdrawn in two outside records; no tower moved, raised or room deleted to force correspondence.",
    "Both source-angle views use the same mesh. Three original plan-core anchors retained; fine glazing, tiny opening shapes/counts, facade details, absolute heights and terrain remain source-informed opaque approximations, not measured reconstruction. B1 external proxy does not claim hidden room fidelity.",
    "Seven material groups preserve Boolean run provenance, not nearest-face painting across material boundaries. No source photograph/plan/PDF/overlay pixels or texture assets embedded. All five views, coordinate plan andthree model-only comparisons personally inspected."
